WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.260 --> 00:00:02.030
Ring Ring Ring Ring Ring!

00:00:02.030 --> 00:00:03.169
Banana Phone!

00:00:03.169 --> 00:00:04.300
Haha, classic.

00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:10.090
We like to have fun over here at SCP explained,
and that’s why today we’ll be talking

00:00:10.090 --> 00:00:14.920
about one of the more sweet and playful anomalies
that the Foundation has in containment.

00:00:14.920 --> 00:00:19.330
If by “sweet” we mean it smells like overripe
fruit and by “playful” we mean carnivorous

00:00:19.330 --> 00:00:24.160
and genetically unstable, then yes, that’s
exactly what’s in store for us.

00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:32.550
Meet SCP-2761 - a mutant hybrid we’ve affectionately
nicknamed Banana-Zilla due the SCP’s retractable

00:00:32.550 --> 00:00:35.680
frill, which resembles the peel of a banana
tree fruit.

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:41.920
Though, at first glance, this part of SCP-2761’s
anomalous anatomy might appear fanciful, like

00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:47.449
something out of a cartoon or children’s
picture book, Bananazilla is no laughing matter,

00:00:47.449 --> 00:00:52.510
and it boasts far fewer novel surprises across
the length of its twelve-meter body.

00:00:52.510 --> 00:00:58.710
The fact is, SCP-2761 could prove an existential
threat to every natural ecosystem on earth

00:00:58.710 --> 00:01:01.710
if it were ever to escape containment.

00:01:01.710 --> 00:01:07.820
The reason for this happens to be SCP-2761’s
infinitely adaptable genetic code which seems

00:01:07.820 --> 00:01:12.280
to constantly evolve in response to its consumption
of other organisms.

00:01:12.280 --> 00:01:19.070
At present, SCP-2761 is amphibious and can
thrive as easily in salt water as it does

00:01:19.070 --> 00:01:22.030
in the freshwater of its containment unit
at Site-71.

00:01:22.030 --> 00:01:27.850
While it does possess gills, they are extremely
small, similar in proportion to those found

00:01:27.850 --> 00:01:30.630
on species in the pipefish subfamily.

00:01:30.630 --> 00:01:34.880
The Foundation’s research into the creature’s
origin has led to the prevailing theory that

00:01:34.880 --> 00:01:40.159
it may have begun its life as an ordinary
pipefish subject to DNA-splicing at a retail

00:01:40.159 --> 00:01:45.759
company known as Aquagene - which specializes
in the sale of genetically modified aquatic

00:01:45.759 --> 00:01:46.979
pets.

00:01:46.979 --> 00:01:53.030
Regardless of its origin, SCP-2761 shares
genotypic and phenotypic traits with over

00:01:53.030 --> 00:01:56.979
five dozen species of flora and fauna aside
from pipefish.

00:01:56.979 --> 00:02:02.040
The majority of these species belong to the
animal kingdom and overwhelmingly tend to

00:02:02.040 --> 00:02:06.710
belong to the amphibian, ray-finned fish,
or reptile classes.

00:02:06.710 --> 00:02:10.770
These borrowed genes express themselves in
a variety of ways, but always in a manner

00:02:10.770 --> 00:02:13.630
that seems beneficial to SCP-2761.

00:02:13.630 --> 00:02:20.280
Bananazilla’s gigantic body is capable of
explosive bursts at speed, much like soft-shelled

00:02:20.280 --> 00:02:24.980
turtles, which, over the course of their natural
evolution, sacrificed more protective armor

00:02:24.980 --> 00:02:26.830
to gain greater mobility.

00:02:26.830 --> 00:02:32.390
For the purpose of detecting prey, Bananazilla
has sixteen barbels - more commonly referred

00:02:32.390 --> 00:02:37.500
to as catfish whiskers - which, like its frill,
are fully retractable.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:44.220
In terms of physical appearance, SCP-2761
has many traits in common with American alligators.

00:02:44.220 --> 00:02:50.780
This includes the over one hundred undifferentiated
conical teeth which SCP-2761 can use to devour

00:02:50.780 --> 00:02:52.080
live prey.

00:02:52.080 --> 00:02:57.530
There are nearly sixty additional rows of
teeth within SCP-2671’s mouth which, on

00:02:57.530 --> 00:03:02.470
the off chance that the hybrid loses any teeth
in the front row, will naturally move forward

00:03:02.470 --> 00:03:03.740
to replace them.

00:03:03.740 --> 00:03:09.430
The process by which SCP-2671 regenerates
lost teeth is nearly identical to that of

00:03:09.430 --> 00:03:14.780
a bull shark, however, the replacement teeth
vary in shape and apparent utility.

00:03:14.780 --> 00:03:19.870
Some rows of bananazilla’s backup teeth
are uniformly serrated and evenly spaced while

00:03:19.870 --> 00:03:25.510
other rows are villiform with prominent, elongated
canines like that of a yellowtail snapper

00:03:25.510 --> 00:03:26.510
fish.

00:03:26.510 --> 00:03:31.480
A dental examination of SCP-2761 revealed
that towards the back of its mouth, there

00:03:31.480 --> 00:03:35.900
were even rows of teeth that bore an uncanny
resemblance to those found within a species

00:03:35.900 --> 00:03:39.950
of great ape: the human species, to be exact.

00:03:39.950 --> 00:03:45.950
The alligator-like claws at the end SPC-2761’s
powerful, compact limbs have sticky pads on

00:03:45.950 --> 00:03:52.360
the underside which have enough adhesive strength
to allow SCP-2761 to climb into trees and

00:03:52.360 --> 00:03:57.670
across other uneven surfaces: such as the
artificial rock wall we’ve provided bananazilla

00:03:57.670 --> 00:04:02.390
in its containment unit for the purpose of
exercise and stimulation.

00:04:02.390 --> 00:04:07.379
These adhesive pads are identical to the ones
found on the toes of green anole lizards,

00:04:07.379 --> 00:04:12.980
which SCP-2761 appears to have inherited other
characteristics from - such as the ability

00:04:12.980 --> 00:04:18.380
to perceive ultraviolet light and limited
color changing for the purpose of camouflage.

00:04:18.380 --> 00:04:23.940
When SCP-2761 was first discovered deep in
the heart of the Florida Everglades, the range

00:04:23.940 --> 00:04:29.040
of its color-changing ability comprised several
shades of green and brown - from a vibrant,

00:04:29.040 --> 00:04:34.580
lustrous green like that of an emerald gemstone
to a dark muddy hue that made it nearly invisible

00:04:34.580 --> 00:04:35.979
in murky water.

00:04:35.979 --> 00:04:39.860
It is believed that the consistent diet of
banana fruit that The Foundation provides

00:04:39.860 --> 00:04:46.360
to SCP-2761 has been able to gradually offset
its camouflage capabilities, inadvertently

00:04:46.360 --> 00:04:51.290
causing it to retain the natural coloration
of bright yellow that it has become known

00:04:51.290 --> 00:04:52.290
for.

00:04:52.290 --> 00:04:58.370
The secret to SCP-2761’s vast amount of
genetic information lies in its cellular structure.

00:04:58.370 --> 00:05:05.250
Each cell in SCP-2761’s bulky body has an
abnormally large nucleus with a primary genome

00:05:05.250 --> 00:05:08.180
made up of hundreds of distinct genes.

00:05:08.180 --> 00:05:12.550
There are additional genomes stored separately
within the nuclei as well, which have been

00:05:12.550 --> 00:05:16.580
heavily scrutinized by research personnel
of Level 3 and above.

00:05:16.580 --> 00:05:22.919
All available data seems to suggest that SCP-2671’s
full genetic code contains the completely

00:05:22.919 --> 00:05:27.020
unaltered genomes of every species it has
ever eaten.

00:05:27.020 --> 00:05:32.120
This includes a diverse microbiome of bacteria
and organic compounds which would be hazardous

00:05:32.120 --> 00:05:36.919
to most other creatures but seem to only affect
the hybrid carnivore’s health in terms of

00:05:36.919 --> 00:05:38.699
conferring benefits.

00:05:38.699 --> 00:05:44.139
Though the various diseases and genetic disorders
that SCP-2761 harbors within its body present

00:05:44.139 --> 00:05:49.810
no safety risk to the SCP itself, any blood-borne
or contagious strains of microscopic life

00:05:49.810 --> 00:05:54.510
are still more than capable of having their
usual adverse effects on other species.

00:05:54.510 --> 00:05:58.810
To prevent the spread of these harmful pathogens,
The Foundation has lined the containment unit

00:05:58.810 --> 00:06:05.370
for SCP-2761 with lead - as the heavy metal
is known to induce anti-microbial activity.

00:06:05.370 --> 00:06:11.770
Despite the tendency for SCP-2761 to undergo
rapid mutation within its primary genome,

00:06:11.770 --> 00:06:16.889
the numerous unaltered genomes within its
cells have never shown signs of independent

00:06:16.889 --> 00:06:17.889
mutation.

00:06:17.889 --> 00:06:22.639
Instead, the unaltered genomes serve a function
that is metaphorically comparable to the extra

00:06:22.639 --> 00:06:26.650
rows of teeth within SCP-2761’s mouth.

00:06:26.650 --> 00:06:30.759
Whenever the primary genome suffers damage
or makes contact with potentially hazardous

00:06:30.759 --> 00:06:37.940
new stimuli, genetic information is transferred
from the unaltered genomes to repair SCP-2761’s

00:06:37.940 --> 00:06:43.509
genetic expression and, in the process, cause
further beneficial mutations to take place.

00:06:43.509 --> 00:06:50.180
In short, SCP-2761 is capable of storing unexpressed
genetic data within its cells, which then

00:06:50.180 --> 00:06:54.919
become apparent in its physical characteristics,
provided that those changes make it fitter

00:06:54.919 --> 00:06:57.669
to survive in its current environment.

00:06:57.669 --> 00:07:02.210
The untapped potential of this advanced form
of genetic rearrangement has become increasingly

00:07:02.210 --> 00:07:04.280
enticing to The Foundation.

00:07:04.280 --> 00:07:08.360
Not unlike the enticing taste of a fresh,
delicious banana.

00:07:08.360 --> 00:07:12.970
As the saying goes, SCP-2761 is what it eats.

00:07:12.970 --> 00:07:18.039
Therefore, it stands to reason that altering
the hybrid’s food intake could, over time,

00:07:18.039 --> 00:07:22.720
lead to a genetic expression that would therein
prove useful to The Foundation’s goals.

00:07:22.720 --> 00:07:28.530
This is especially true when the mutable properties
of SCP-2761 are compared to those of a similar

00:07:28.530 --> 00:07:33.690
but far more dangerous reptilian SCP - the
infamous SCP-682.

00:07:33.690 --> 00:07:40.590
While SCP-682 is nearly impossible to destroy
due to its instantaneous adaptation, the changes

00:07:40.590 --> 00:07:46.210
to its physiology recede and disappear when
no longer required to ensure its survival.

00:07:46.210 --> 00:07:51.879
SCP-2761, on the other hand, retains the sum
total of every useful feature it has gleaned

00:07:51.879 --> 00:07:53.400
from its diet.

00:07:53.400 --> 00:07:59.770
Presently, SCP-2761 possesses barely a fraction
of SCP-682’s overall strength and destructive

00:07:59.770 --> 00:08:04.180
capability, but if raised properly within
a long enough time frame, with a steady and

00:08:04.180 --> 00:08:09.490
balanced diet of the optimal anomalous and
non-anomalous organisms, it is theorized that

00:08:09.490 --> 00:08:15.620
SCP-2761 could molded into the ideal countermeasure
for its reptilian rival.

00:08:15.620 --> 00:08:20.740
And most crucially to the plan, because Bananazilla
hunts only out of the carnivorous instinct

00:08:20.740 --> 00:08:25.790
for sustenance and survival, it lacks any
of the malice towards other life which defines

00:08:25.790 --> 00:08:29.590
the twisted Joker-like psychology of the hard-to-destroy
reptile.

00:08:29.590 --> 00:08:35.660
If this desirable outcome were somehow to
be achieved, the final containment of SCP-682

00:08:35.660 --> 00:08:40.200
would be all but assured - even if its total
and permanent destruction remained forever

00:08:40.200 --> 00:08:42.330
out of The Foundation’s reach.

00:08:42.330 --> 00:08:48.430
For now, even the notion of broadening SCP-2671’s
diet has been deemed to be far too risky to

00:08:48.430 --> 00:08:49.430
attempt.

00:08:49.430 --> 00:08:53.529
Even a mouth-watering jumbo-sized bucket of
seemingly harmless non-specific restaurant

00:08:53.529 --> 00:08:59.040
brand chicken wings could cause the hybrid
to develop razor-sharp talons, a highly-disturbing

00:08:59.040 --> 00:09:04.740
morning call, or an unforeseen boost in intelligence
that might aid it in escaping containment.

00:09:04.740 --> 00:09:08.210
Not to mention the possible spread of avian
influenza.

00:09:08.210 --> 00:09:12.870
Though the finer details regarding Bananazilla’s
genetics are known only to sufficiently high-ranking

00:09:12.870 --> 00:09:18.320
members of the genetic research team, rumors
have circulated throughout site-71 that this

00:09:18.320 --> 00:09:24.010
humble SCP may still prove to be an incredible
asset in another way if the highly adaptable

00:09:24.010 --> 00:09:27.860
cells within its body can somehow be replicated.

00:09:27.860 --> 00:09:32.560
This has recently been the obsession of one
Dr. Scapelli, who as an avid reader of comic

00:09:32.560 --> 00:09:38.450
books and manga, has hypothesized - or more
accurately fantasized - that the human genome

00:09:38.450 --> 00:09:44.230
could be augmented through the integration
of transplanted cells from SCP-2761.

00:09:44.230 --> 00:09:48.769
In Scapelli’s eyes, which by all estimates
are filled with a naive optimism generally

00:09:48.769 --> 00:09:53.920
unexpected in a Level 3 researcher, a successful
transplant could turn a regular human being

00:09:53.920 --> 00:09:59.260
into a highly-adaptable mutant super being:
able to become stronger with every meal.

00:09:59.260 --> 00:10:04.670
Amidst the persistent worry of his scientific
peers, Dr. Scapelli has, in his off-duty hours,

00:10:04.670 --> 00:10:08.709
drafted unofficial plans for what he believes
could be the greatest mobile task force The

00:10:08.709 --> 00:10:10.840
Foundation has ever known.

00:10:10.840 --> 00:10:16.490
These heroic warriors would be given the designation
Mobile Task Force Tau-68, but all the villains

00:10:16.490 --> 00:10:21.160
in the world would know and fear them by their
clever and ingenious code name:

00:10:21.160 --> 00:10:22.480
The Banana Splits!

00:10:22.480 --> 00:10:27.350
While every recipient of a successful bananazilla
cell transplant would be allowed into the

00:10:27.350 --> 00:10:32.850
group, a core team of specialists would be
chosen to embody Dr. Scapelli’s wildly imaginative

00:10:32.850 --> 00:10:35.910
and yet incredibly specific tastes.

00:10:35.910 --> 00:10:40.089
Standing at the top of the food chain would
be the task force’s chief commander: Apex

00:10:40.089 --> 00:10:41.089
Man!

00:10:41.089 --> 00:10:45.120
With an all-meat diet consisting of the most
deadly predators from around the globe, Apex

00:10:45.120 --> 00:10:49.860
Man would “bear” the responsibilities
of leadership, “badger” the bad guys,

00:10:49.860 --> 00:10:55.860
“wolf” down all “snakes in the grass”,
and “crocodile rock” the world into everlasting

00:10:55.860 --> 00:11:00.570
peace with his “eagle”-litarian ways,
and he’s not “lion”.

00:11:00.570 --> 00:11:02.050
Okay, we’ll stop…

00:11:02.050 --> 00:11:07.290
For now.

00:11:07.290 --> 00:11:12.040
Apex Man’s loyal second-in-command would
be Honey Girl, empowered by the environmental

00:11:12.040 --> 00:11:15.990
DNA of thousands of pollinated plants and
the bees that tend to them.

00:11:15.990 --> 00:11:19.800
This graceful soldier of justice would have
The Foundation’s enemies sneezing for mercy

00:11:19.800 --> 00:11:22.440
with her countless allergenic attacks.

00:11:22.440 --> 00:11:24.079
Flower power, indeed!

00:11:24.079 --> 00:11:29.139
Next, of course, would be The Lord of Sea
- a pescatarian who’s always part shellfish

00:11:29.139 --> 00:11:32.600
but never a bit selfish when it comes to saving
the day!

00:11:32.600 --> 00:11:37.450
His powerful retractable tentacles would squeeze
the fight out of even the most wicked villain,

00:11:37.450 --> 00:11:41.970
and with shark-like teeth of his own: he’d
never fail to take a bite out of anomalous

00:11:41.970 --> 00:11:42.970
crime.

00:11:42.970 --> 00:11:45.700
Watching over the team from the skies is Wild
Turkey!

00:11:45.700 --> 00:11:49.470
Gobbling up important reconnaissance data
as quickly as he gobbles up his favorite poultry

00:11:49.470 --> 00:11:54.920
dishes, this bad birdman is here to give evildoers
a “fowl” time.

00:11:54.920 --> 00:11:59.730
Last but not least would be the teen tofu
titan himself: The Cube.

00:11:59.730 --> 00:12:01.270
One hundred percent boy.

00:12:01.270 --> 00:12:03.370
One hundred percent soy.

00:12:03.370 --> 00:12:09.280
Dr. Scapelli’s eventual proposal for Mobile
Task Force Tau-68 was met with uproarious

00:12:09.280 --> 00:12:13.970
laughter and was unanimously turned down by
every Level 3 and higher personnel who was

00:12:13.970 --> 00:12:15.570
present to hear it.

00:12:15.570 --> 00:12:20.329
O5-1 actually gave him ten bucks afterwards,
as thanks for giving him such a good giggle.

00:12:20.329 --> 00:12:22.970
Dr. Scapelli was not pleased.

00:12:22.970 --> 00:12:28.230
Disgraced and humiliated, Dr. Scapelli chose
to take a lengthy sabbatical from Site-71.

00:12:28.230 --> 00:12:33.200
But as he packed up his notes for Mobile Task
Force Tau-68 - which included several pencil

00:12:33.200 --> 00:12:37.360
and paper illustrations he had done by hand
- the researcher was overcome with a sense

00:12:37.360 --> 00:12:38.990
of righteous purpose.

00:12:38.990 --> 00:12:43.089
The Banana Splits were an idea so brilliant
that he just couldn’t give up on them.

00:12:43.089 --> 00:12:49.100
If the Foundation wouldn’t help Dr. Scapelli
realize his dream, he had an idea who would.

00:12:49.100 --> 00:12:53.529
On the night before he departed from Site-71,
Scapelli used his authority as a member of

00:12:53.529 --> 00:13:00.120
Level 3 personnel to access the research lab
and secure a DNA sample from SCP-2761.

00:13:00.120 --> 00:13:04.579
He proceeded to erase any and all records
of him having entered the lab that night.

00:13:04.579 --> 00:13:10.120
Without any further delay, Dr. Scapelli booked
a nonstop flight to the sunshine state of

00:13:10.120 --> 00:13:11.120
Florida.

00:13:11.120 --> 00:13:15.579
He had one destination in mind: the Orlando
regional headquarters of Aquagene.

00:13:15.579 --> 00:13:19.899
Surely, the company responsible for accidentally
creating bananazilla would understand the

00:13:19.899 --> 00:13:23.829
importance of using their genetic research
for the betterment of the world.

00:13:23.829 --> 00:13:28.640
Yes, of course, they would understand, Scapelli
thought to himself as he fell asleep on the

00:13:28.640 --> 00:13:29.640
plane.

00:13:29.640 --> 00:13:33.589
While he napped, Dr. Scapelli dreamed of the
glorious day that his secret Mobile Task Force

00:13:33.589 --> 00:13:39.010
would save the world and prove everyone who
ever doubted him to be totally in the wrong.

00:13:39.010 --> 00:13:44.800
In the dream, several dangerous SCPs had escaped
containment, including SCP-058: The Heart

00:13:44.800 --> 00:13:45.930
of Darkness.

00:13:45.930 --> 00:13:50.720
The Keter-class monstrosity was on a brutal
rampage throughout its containment facility,

00:13:50.720 --> 00:13:54.660
lashing out with its horrifying tendrils at
any personnel within reach.

00:13:54.660 --> 00:13:59.209
Just when all hope seemed lost, Dr. Scapelli
would arrive with Mobile Task Force Tau-68

00:13:59.209 --> 00:14:00.209
in tow.

00:14:00.209 --> 00:14:04.610
All of the coolest and strongest members of
the super team were standing at his side,

00:14:04.610 --> 00:14:10.589
ready for action: Apex Man, Honey Girl, The
Lord of Sea, Wild Turkey, and The Cube.

00:14:10.589 --> 00:14:12.449
“Banana Splits, Assemble!”

00:14:12.449 --> 00:14:15.209
Dr. Scapelli’s dream self shouted.

00:14:15.209 --> 00:14:20.500
His genetically-modified heroes proceeded
to bring the ultimate smackdown to SCP-058.

00:14:20.500 --> 00:14:25.370
From the palms of her hands, Honey Girl unleashed
viscous globs of her namesake substance which

00:14:25.370 --> 00:14:30.490
stuck The Heart of Darkness’ arthropod legs
to the floor: holding it in place.

00:14:30.490 --> 00:14:34.650
As expected, the heart began to launch into
one of its unnerving speeches thought to drive

00:14:34.650 --> 00:14:39.029
listeners to madness, but Wild Turkey made
gobbling noises at the top of his lungs to

00:14:39.029 --> 00:14:40.519
drown out the sound.

00:14:40.519 --> 00:14:46.050
Trapped and effectively silenced but not defeated,
SCP-058’s thrashing tentacles were still

00:14:46.050 --> 00:14:50.910
a major problem - until The Lord of The Sea
extended his own tentacles to match the monster

00:14:50.910 --> 00:14:52.079
blow for blow.

00:14:52.079 --> 00:14:56.540
Finally, Apex Man’s grizzly bear DNA could
no longer resist the honey-covered heart in

00:14:56.540 --> 00:15:02.339
front of him, and he closed in on SCP-058
to crush it with the granddaddy of bear hugs

00:15:02.339 --> 00:15:05.050
before scarfing it down with a noisy crunch.

00:15:05.050 --> 00:15:08.889
The Heart of Darkness was beaten and eaten
in that order.

00:15:08.889 --> 00:15:13.860
The other researchers cheered and clapped
for Dr. Scapelli and for his Banana Splits.

00:15:13.860 --> 00:15:18.089
Overcome with unconditional praise the likes
of which Dr. Scapelli had never experienced,

00:15:18.089 --> 00:15:20.579
everyone around him began to chant his name:

00:15:20.579 --> 00:15:21.579
“Scapelli!

00:15:21.579 --> 00:15:22.579
Scapelli!

00:15:22.579 --> 00:15:23.579
Scapelli!”

00:15:23.579 --> 00:15:28.019
The dream version of Apex Man approached Dr.
Scapelli and gave his creator a congratulatory

00:15:28.019 --> 00:15:29.259
pat on the back.

00:15:29.259 --> 00:15:35.079
“Those who hide unwanted things in the fog
must eternally reckon with the afterimage

00:15:35.079 --> 00:15:39.949
of his twilight’s sinful longing,” said
Apex Man in the vocal tone and accent of an

00:15:39.949 --> 00:15:41.529
elderly British man.

00:15:41.529 --> 00:15:45.110
He proceeded to sprout four tentacles similar
to those of SCP-058.

00:15:45.110 --> 00:15:50.160
Dr. Scapelli jolted awake with a scream, only
to see that he was the last one still aboard

00:15:50.160 --> 00:15:51.220
his plane.

00:15:51.220 --> 00:15:55.959
An irritated flight attendant told the researcher
that the flight had touched down at Orlando

00:15:55.959 --> 00:16:00.420
National Airport, and that he needed to grab
his carry-on luggage and exit the aircraft

00:16:00.420 --> 00:16:01.550
immediately.

00:16:01.550 --> 00:16:03.870
Scapelli didn’t need to be told twice.

00:16:03.870 --> 00:16:07.649
He made a beeline out of the airport and called
a cab to take him to the resort he had booked

00:16:07.649 --> 00:16:08.710
for his stay.

00:16:08.710 --> 00:16:13.541
After settling into a hotel room, the researcher
made a few phone calls, and before long, he

00:16:13.541 --> 00:16:18.370
was able to secure an impromptu meeting with
two of the scientists in Aquagene’s employ:

00:16:18.370 --> 00:16:22.090
Dr. Pearl Watkins and Dr. Marcus Nakamura.

00:16:22.090 --> 00:16:26.519
Both Watkins and Nakamura had been previously
contacted by Foundation researcher Mathew

00:16:26.519 --> 00:16:29.850
Liu, under the guise of a meeting with the
EPA.

00:16:29.850 --> 00:16:33.829
The Foundation had been keeping tabs on them
since then while maintaining their cover.

00:16:33.829 --> 00:16:39.800
While the scientists had assisted in the successful
containment of SCP-2761, the potential of

00:16:39.800 --> 00:16:45.160
Aquagene’s genetic technology needed to
be monitored in the event of further anomalous

00:16:45.160 --> 00:16:46.160
creations.

00:16:46.160 --> 00:16:49.910
It wasn’t difficult for Dr. Scapelli to
insert himself into the narrative that Aquagene

00:16:49.910 --> 00:16:55.390
already believed: posing as another agent
of the EPA looking to inspect the company’s

00:16:55.390 --> 00:16:56.390
policies.

00:16:56.390 --> 00:17:00.279
Of course, since he was operating without
the permission of the Foundation, Dr. Scapelli

00:17:00.279 --> 00:17:04.039
made sure that the meeting was held at Aquagene
Headquarters.

00:17:04.039 --> 00:17:08.770
Watkins and Nakamura were apprehensive enough,
given the scrutiny that researcher Liu had

00:17:08.770 --> 00:17:12.980
put them under in their first meeting, and
became increasingly alarmed as Dr. Scapelli

00:17:12.980 --> 00:17:18.760
presented them with the SCP-2761 sample as
well as his “creative” pitch.

00:17:18.760 --> 00:17:20.650
“It would be a superhero group!

00:17:20.650 --> 00:17:21.890
Like in the movies!”

00:17:21.890 --> 00:17:25.780
Dr. Scapelli exclaimed, having just spoken
at length about the viability of Mobile Task

00:17:25.780 --> 00:17:27.429
Force Tau-68.

00:17:27.429 --> 00:17:30.300
The Aquagene employees exchanged terror-stricken
looks.

00:17:30.300 --> 00:17:32.320
Nakamura was the first to speak:

00:17:32.320 --> 00:17:34.419
“It is a tempting offer…”

00:17:34.419 --> 00:17:38.539
Marcus begun, trying to be polite “...but
our budget is stretched thin enough as it

00:17:38.539 --> 00:17:39.539
is.

00:17:39.539 --> 00:17:40.539
Your project…”

00:17:40.539 --> 00:17:42.890
He jumped with shock as Dr. Scapelli cut him
off mid sentence:

00:17:42.890 --> 00:17:44.200
“Don’t worry about the funding!

00:17:44.200 --> 00:17:45.520
I can cover it out of pocket.

00:17:45.520 --> 00:17:49.570
Sure, I may have to take out a loan and possibly
apply for unemployment, but isn't saving the

00:17:49.570 --> 00:17:51.280
world worth any price?”

00:17:51.280 --> 00:17:55.800
Watkins responded: “We try to do things
very carefully here, Agent Scapelli.

00:17:55.800 --> 00:17:59.660
I’ll be blunt, what you’re describing
is far beyond the scope of our research, and

00:17:59.660 --> 00:18:02.770
using live human test subjects for this seems
highly unethical.”

00:18:02.770 --> 00:18:03.770
“Unethical?”

00:18:03.770 --> 00:18:05.549
Dr. Scapelli said, baffled.

00:18:05.549 --> 00:18:08.590
“What could possibly be unethical about
giving people to fight evil?”

00:18:08.590 --> 00:18:11.340
“I think what Pearl is trying to say is…”

00:18:11.340 --> 00:18:12.510
Nakura chimed in.

00:18:12.510 --> 00:18:14.420
“...this all seems a bit naive.”

00:18:14.420 --> 00:18:17.620
Dr. Scapelli sunk into his chair, feeling
defeated.

00:18:17.620 --> 00:18:21.850
First, the Foundation had rejected his idea,
and now Aquagene too.

00:18:21.850 --> 00:18:25.300
Perhaps it really was time to give up on Mobile
Task Force Tau-68.

00:18:25.300 --> 00:18:30.909
If he pressed his luck any further at Aquagene,
word could get back to Site-71, and he’d

00:18:30.909 --> 00:18:35.179
have to kiss his career at The Foundation
goodbye - and potentially his memories, if

00:18:35.179 --> 00:18:39.730
they decided to give him a hefty dose of Amnestics
as part of his severance package.

00:18:39.730 --> 00:18:43.780
Later that night in the resort restaurant,
Dr. Scapelli was crying into his plate of

00:18:43.780 --> 00:18:44.780
food.

00:18:44.780 --> 00:18:48.270
His dreams of creating the world’s first
superhero team had been crushed that day,

00:18:48.270 --> 00:18:52.020
and he still had the rest of his sabbatical
to spend in Florida.

00:18:52.020 --> 00:18:57.150
As he tried to eat his steak, he was reminded
of Apex Man and broke down into tears all

00:18:57.150 --> 00:18:58.150
over again.

00:18:58.150 --> 00:19:01.850
The other restaurant patrons were beginning
to stare at Dr. Scapelli, and he was about

00:19:01.850 --> 00:19:06.830
to consider leaving when a man in dark shades
approached his table and sat down across from

00:19:06.830 --> 00:19:07.830
him.

00:19:07.830 --> 00:19:11.600
The man waited for Scapelli to cease his weeping
before formally introducing himself as Dr.

00:19:11.600 --> 00:19:12.900
Gregory Higgins.

00:19:12.900 --> 00:19:17.340
He claimed to be a former employee of Aquagene,
and had used insider information from an old

00:19:17.340 --> 00:19:21.190
colleague to learn about Dr. Scapelli’s
meeting with Watkins and Nakamura.

00:19:21.190 --> 00:19:25.049
By tracing the call from the resort earlier
that afternoon, it wasn’t that difficult

00:19:25.049 --> 00:19:26.850
to track the Foundation researcher down.

00:19:26.850 --> 00:19:29.140
“Are you going to call me naive too?”

00:19:29.140 --> 00:19:31.039
Scapelli said in a huff.

00:19:31.039 --> 00:19:34.020
“Far from it,” Higgins replied, wearing
a mischievous grin.

00:19:34.020 --> 00:19:36.070
“I think your idea has potential.”

00:19:36.070 --> 00:19:37.210
“You really mean it?”

00:19:37.210 --> 00:19:38.820
Scapelli’s face lit up.

00:19:38.820 --> 00:19:39.820
Higgins laughed.

00:19:39.820 --> 00:19:40.820
“Of course.

00:19:40.820 --> 00:19:41.820
But then again… what do I know?

00:19:41.820 --> 00:19:44.270
I’m just the guy who created that Bananazilla!”

00:19:44.270 --> 00:19:48.910
He continued: “…It was a complete accident,
of course, but I think we could really make

00:19:48.910 --> 00:19:53.020
Pearl and Marcus regret ever doubting us if
this superhero thing goes the way you think

00:19:53.020 --> 00:19:54.020
it will.”

00:19:54.020 --> 00:19:55.429
Dr. Scapelli smiled.

00:19:55.429 --> 00:19:58.990
“Higgins, this is the beginning of a beautiful
partnership.”

00:19:58.990 --> 00:20:03.299
The two genetic scientists - one formerly
of the Foundation and the other formerly of

00:20:03.299 --> 00:20:07.210
Aquagene - laughed in shared joy at the things
they might soon accomplish.

00:20:07.210 --> 00:20:13.179
There were only two words to describe the
chaos that might ensue from the combined imagination

00:20:13.179 --> 00:20:16.800
of this couple of mad geniuses: totally bananas!

00:20:16.800 --> 00:20:23.380
Now go check out “SCP-682 - Ways SCP Foundation
Tried to Kill Hard To Destroy Reptile” and

00:20:23.380 --> 00:20:29.170
“SCP-6415 - Tragedy of the Reptile Man”
for more fascinating reptilian anomalies!

